{"step_index":207,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:11:35Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 2 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. showing an already created app \n2. Improve the existing StreamWave Entertainment interface without rebuilding the project or changing its working FastAPI backend.\r\n\r\nFirst inspect the current files and understand how the interface, catalogue API, filtering, media details, playback and event logging work. Preserve all existing API endpoints, data structures, tests, Vercel configuration and working functionality.\r\n\r\nMake only the following interface improvements:\r\n\r\n1. PLAYBACK LABELS\r\n\r\n* Movie cards must display “Watch Preview”.\r\n* Music cards must display “Play Sample”.\r\n* The featured-content button must use the correct label according to its media type.\r\n* Do not use “Play Demo” on every card.\r\n* If multiple catalogue items use the same generated demonstration file, show a discreet “Technical sample” label and do not imply that copyrighted content is being streamed.\r\n\r\n2. HEADER\r\n\r\n* Reduce the visual size of the “Serverless Demonstration” badge.\r\n* Keep it visible because it is important for the academic assessment.\r\n<truncated 3519 bytes>\n3. Update the existing StreamWave FastAPI project so that the completed five-second StreamWave MP4 video is used as the preview for every movie when a user clicks “Watch Preview”.\r\n\r\nDo not rebuild the application or replace its working FastAPI backend. First inspect the existing project structure, catalogue data, playback buttons, modal system and `/api/play-events` endpoint.\r\n\r\nIMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS\r\n\r\n1. VIDEO ASSET\r\n\r\n* Locate the completed five-second StreamWave MP4 file I have added to the project.\r\n* If it is not already in the correct static directory, place it in:\r\n  `public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\r\n* Do not modify, regenerate or compress the original video unless browser playback fails because of an unsupported format.\r\n* Use the relative public URL:\r\n  `/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\r\n* The browser must retrieve the video directly as a static asset. Do not proxy video bytes through FastAPI.\r\n\r\n2. MOVIE CATALOGUE\r\n\r\n* Configure every item whose media type is `movie` to use the same S\n<truncated 3528 bytes>\n4. put this as the logo of the streaming company\n5. make it a bit bigger if its possible \n6. just say watch dont watch preview and also just say play dont say play sample  \n7. also change that icon to the streaming icon \n8. change the this icon to the company logo to the company logo \n9. LETS also have a landing page similar to netflix one which will allow users to either login or get started with the name of the streaming company \n10. Extend the existing StreamWave FastAPI/Vercel project by adding an original landing page, simulated subscription-payment process and paid-member access control.\r\n\r\nDo not rebuild or break the existing catalogue, music player, five-second movie preview, playback logging, API documentation or Vercel configuration. Inspect the existing project before changing anything.\r\n\r\nThis is an academic demonstration. Do not integrate a real payment gateway, transfer money or collect real financial information.\r\n\r\nLANDING PAGE\r\n\r\n1. Make `/` the public landing page and the first page encountered by visitors.\r\n2. Use the existing StreamWave logo and dark graphite, white and red brand colours.\r\n3. Use the supplied streaming-service screenshot only as inspiration for visual hierarchy. Do not copy Netflix branding, wording, copyrighted posters or exact layout.\r\n4. Create an original hero section using existing StreamWave catalogue artwork with a dark overlay.\r\n5. Use this main copy:\r\n\r\n   * Heading: “Zimbabwe’s stories,\n<truncated 5409 bytes>\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Session Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n- **Extend StreamWave Platform with Subscription Payment Simulation & Paid-Member Access Control**:\n  - *User Original Intent*: \"Extend the existing StreamWave FastAPI/Vercel project by adding an original landing page, simulated subscription-payment process and paid-member access control. Do not rebuild or break the existing catalogue, music player, five-second movie preview, playback logging, API documentation or Vercel configuration.\"\n  - *Current Status*: **IMPLEMENTATION** (Backend endpoints in `app.py`, Landing page `public/index.html`, Checkout page `public/checkout.html`, Library page `public/library.html`, and CSS `public/css/styles.css` are created. Next step: update `public/js/app.js` and extend `tests/test_api.py` to achieve 100% test verification).\n  - *Sub-tasks*:\n    - **Public Landing Page (`/`)**: Must feature heading *\"Zimbabwe’s stories, music and movies — all in one place.\"*, supporting text *\"Stream from US$2.99 per month. Cancel anytime.\"*, and instruction *\"Enter your email address to start your StreamWave membership.\"*. Includes logo, Sign In button, email field, Get Started button, benefits section, how it works section, supported payment methods section, and academic footer.\n    - **Single Subscription Configuration**: Store `StreamWave Monthly` ($2.99/mo) in one central configuration location (`app.py` `SUBSCRIPTION_PLAN`).\n    - **Checkout Page (`/checkout`)**: Prominent warning banner *\"ACADEMIC PAYMENT SIMULATION — No real money will be charged. Do not enter genuine payment information.\"*, subscription summary, EcoCash test number (`077 000 0000`), Visa test card (`4242`), MasterCard test card (`4444`), visual step progress animations. Send ONLY `email`, `method`, and `plan_id` to backend. Never 